/-!
# The original module in the terminal binary-linear branch

The literal subgroups M₁, U, Kᵢ and Qᵢ and the C.2.7 star marking are
kept distinct. Conjugation constructs the X/O₂(X)-action on U itself;
Sylow averaging proves generation by U∩ZS. This excludes the natural-dual
row with its source K-containment and S₃-square quotient.

For the orthogonal row, the actual two-core identity and a best FF*
offender on U are constructed. The original seed marks the permutation
stabilizer, and the source Sylow order and cubic rank place the transported
offender inside the concrete core excluded by B.3.2(6). The literal four-row
consumer consequently leaves only repeated-natural and exterior-five.

For repeated-natural, cubic rank excludes degree four. Sylow averaging
identifies C_X(U∩ZS) with M₁, and the original action marks its image as
the degree-five point parabolic. The literal residual maps then construct
K_I/O₂(K_I) ≅ SL₄(2), retained with the action in the row consumer.
For exterior-five, the original M₁ image is the 2+3 parabolic, giving
K_I/O₂(K_I) ≅ C₃ × SL₃(2). The original O^{3′}(O₂,₃(K_I)) has a quotient
of order three and three-rank one. The earlier identity X=O^{3′}(I)
makes it T-invariant. Projection to SL₃(2) proves that its intersection
with K has three-rank one. This gives a proper nontrivial T-invariant
subgroup of K/O₂(K), contradicting the earlier T-irreducibility clause.
The literal consumer now leaves only the degree-five repeated-natural row.

C.2.7 now classifies the actual original U: reducedness and full movement
identify the B.5 moved carrier, and the literal quotient maps match its action
with the canonical X/O₂(X)-action. The final consumer therefore constructs
the row premise internally.

The repeated-natural source consumer now constructs the minimal parabolic
inside X and its two-perfect residual Y₁ in NI outside MI. The original
S-action is retained, with Y₁S/O₂(Y₁S) ≅ S₃. The actual S₃-square quotient
proves S-reducibility, and Kc centralization identifies KI with Kc.
Corrected 15.2.21(1),(3) now excludes this seed. The small-action dependency
also derives the KS quotient from the natural-five point action and proves
T-irreducibility from the original wreath quotient.

Source exports the final binary-branch contradiction. It derives component
escape from intrinsic movement and applies the completed small-action
argument on the literal groups and quotient maps. Its selected-component
consumer constructs the marked parabolic and faithful NI action from the
original star model, without an additional KS quotient premise. The earlier
plane geometry, HStar quotients, Kc orbit, restricted actions, plane involution
and no-chi statements remain for their source producers and final
plane-uniqueness assembly; the terminal module exclusions are complete.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 15.2.23, printed pp.1116--1117.
-/
